inine and neuter forms of  they them and their in other words the  third person plural for mixed groups the  neuter is used this sentence is svo  subject verb object but it's more  precise to refer to icelandic as a v2  language the verb is the second element  in the sentence or clause that's the  case for basically all germanic  languages except for modern english  this sentence could also be  michael m called i  but as happens generally in germanic  languages the word order is verb subject  in yes or no questions  is your name michael literally are  called you michael notice that the  subject thu becomes voiced zlu and is  suffixed to the verb in writing  nice to meet you word for word it's  pleasure to become acquainted with you  means pleasure or fun its old english  equivalent was gamin which evolved into  the modern english word game  is the particle used before a verb's  infinitive form so it's translated here  as tu but it's a cognate of the english  word at  kindest may appear to be related to the  english word no but it's actually  distantly related to the english word  can which in old english kunan used to  mean no and its current meaning  developed from the sense of know how to  the active verb is  to make known or introduce  this form with st is used reflexively to  become acquainted with  this is the dative form of the personal  pronoun meaning you in the singular the  dative case is used to show someone is  receiving the action rather than being  the direct object of it  quite a close setting where is the  restroom word for word where is restroom  is a cognate of the english word where  looks like r in english right well  they're related it's a form of the verb  meaning be  but vera looks more like a were than b  doesn't it they're related in english  the infinitive to be and other forms  with b come from a different old english  verb baeon but the past tense and  present tense forms come from old  english weisan a cognate of vesa or wesa  an earlier